# Error Handling

## Repository contract

Repositories return `suspend fun (): Result<T>` (see `mobile-data-layer.mdc`). They never throw to the caller.

```kotlin
override suspend fun getGuides(): Result<List<Guide>> = coRunCatching(
    tryBlock = { apiClient.getGuides().getOrThrow().guides.map { it.toDomain() } },
    catchBlock = { throwable ->
        Napier.e(throwable = throwable, message = "GuidesRepositoryImpl.getGuides failed")
        throwable.wrapResultFailure()
    },
)
```

## Discipline

- In `suspend` code, use `coRunCatching { ... }` from `common/extensions/CoroutineExtensions.kt`. It rethrows `CancellationException` and converts other throwables to `Result.failure`. Optional second parameter `catchBlock: (Throwable) -> Result<T>` defaults to `{ it.wrapResultFailure() }`.
- Plain `runCatching` is only acceptable in **non-suspend** call paths.
- Repositories log via `Napier.e(throwable = ..., message = ...)` in their catch blocks; presentation code does not swallow errors silently. Executors log on failure paths via `Napier.e(...)` before dispatching `Message.SetError(true)`.

## Executor layer

Executors fold `Result<T>` into `Message`s for the Reducer and (when appropriate) `Label`s for the UI:

```kotlin
guidesRepository.getGuides()
    .onSuccess { dispatch(Message.SetGuides(it)) }
    .onFailure { throwable ->
        Napier.e(throwable = throwable, message = "GuidesExecutor#loadGuides failed")
        dispatch(Message.SetError(true))
    }
```

Executors do not throw past the `BaseExecutor` boundary — every failure becomes a `Message` (and optionally a `Label`).

## ViewModel / UI layer

ViewModels never log errors — logging is a data-layer / executor responsibility. The UI renders `Ui*State.isError` and routes one-shot effects through `Ui*Label`. `println()` is forbidden — use `Napier.v / d / i / w / e`.

## Logging

Napier is initialized once per platform entry with `Napier.base(DebugAntilog(...))` before `initKoin(...)`. The call appends antilogs — if an entry can be re-created (test scenarios), wrap with `Napier.takeLogarithm()` first to avoid duplicate sinks.
